@local/dsh-image README · dsh-image：Image generation for DeepSeek Harness through an OpenAI-compatible relay
(configured for `api.ykh.ai` / `gpt-image-2`).

No dependencies, no build step.

@local/dsh-image README · What it registers：The command's result is UI-side and never enters model history, so `/image`
costs no tokens. The tool's result does enter the conversation, which is what
lets the model show the picture and keep working.

@local/dsh-image README · The Settings section：DSH's Settings dialog carries an **Image Generation** nav entry (registered
through the settings shell's `settings.section` slot, the same mechanism
dsh-better-sidebar uses). It edits:

@local/dsh-image README · The Settings section：> Editing the same fields by hand in the profile patch still works — both
> paths write the same volatile layer, and a revision mismatch is resolved by
> reloading the form.

@local/dsh-image README · Response shapes：The shape actually used is reported in the tool result, the log line and the
command summary, so a first run resolves the question instead of us guessing.
`test/relay.test.mjs` covers all three plus the failure modes.
